#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0214 expect=violation domain=TE
#note "TEDUR is an ISO-8601 duration STRING -- type=Char, never Num. Row 1 populates TEENRL; row 2 leaves BOTH empty -> FIRES. Both columns are PRESENT here so BroadcastFold stays UNKNOWN on both halves and the row loop decides, giving a per-record count of 1. The pin ends with TWO trailing '=' signs and they are load-bearing: a pin may legally end in an empty value and deleting the '=' changes the assertion."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 ETCD=TRT TEENRL= TEDUR=
dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
col TEENRL  type=Char label="Rule for End of Element"
col TEDUR   type=Char label="Planned Duration of Element"
---
S1 | TE | SCRN | Screening | Informed consent | End of screening | 
S1 | TE | TRT  | Treatment | First dose       |                  | 
---
